{
  "manufacturer": "Kohler",
  "manufacturer_slug": "kohler",
  "model": "Decision-Maker 3500 generator set controller",
  "model_slug": "decision-maker-3500",
  "short_model": "DM3500",
  "aliases": [
    "Decision-Maker 3500",
    "DEC3500",
    "DEC 3500"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Generator controller",
  "applies_to": "Kohler Decision-Maker 3500 generator set controllers (Modbus map version 2; some registers need firmware 1.4 or later), Modbus RTU on RS-485.",
  "summary": "The Decision-Maker 3500 is a Kohler generator set controller whose map also carries bus, synchronizing and generator management data. Its Modbus RTU map reports generator and bus electrical values as percentages of the set's ratings, engine data, run-time counters, genset state and master switch position, plus event logs and configuration. This map covers the electrical, engine, run-time, rating and status registers.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "The manual prints 6-digit holding-register references (400001 = first holding register; 409999 is register 49999 in 5-digit form), so 400001 is wire address 0 and 400652 is wire address 651."
  },
  "default_word_order": "CDAB",
  "firmware": "Map version 2; firmware 1.4 or later for some registers",
  "source": {
    "title": "Modbus Communications Protocol Operation (generator set, transfer switch and power monitor controllers)",
    "doc_number": "TP-6113 12/21p",
    "revision_date": "2021-12",
    "url": "https://resources.kohler.com/power/kohler/industrial/pdf/tp6113.pdf",
    "pages": "Serial settings and data types pp. 15-16; function and exception codes p. 17; DM3500 setup pp. 81-82; registers pp. 83-103; registers 400652/400653 and invalid-data values p. 104"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Generator and bus voltages, currents and powers are reported as percent of the set's rated values (x100), not volts, amps or kW. Rated current is at 400108 and the kW rating at 400109; the rated voltage is the system voltage at 400105.",
    "32-bit UDINT counters are split into an LW register followed by an HW register, so they are listed CDAB.",
    "Left out: 400087-400088 (the low word is labelled controller total operation time while the high word is labelled unloaded hours), per-phase reactive and apparent power, phase angles, speed/voltage bias, the voltage/resistance/digital channel configuration blocks, time delays, protective relay and synchronizer settings, load management, generator management, event logs and the ID strings.",
    "Invalid-data flags: 0xFFC0 = register not supported in this application; 0x7FE0-0x7FFF = supported but the value is unknown (for example ECM sensors with the ECM unpowered).",
    "Registers marked in the manual as needing firmware 1.4 or later return errors on older firmware."
  ],
